Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-19-2001||01:02 PM||||Whats the easiest,quickest & Cheapest v8 swap?<P>I have a 2.8l in my 84SC now, and thinking of something with more guts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>I have full access to a garage with a pit,hoist, and welding supplies.. <P>I would be picking up the motor as a drop-in prob out of a smashed car,<P>would the caddy 4.9 be my best idea?<P><BR>I would perfer to keep it carberated and not FI..<P><BR>Thanks for any info  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||onfire||08-19-2001||01:06 PM||||I here the 4.5 caddy motor is easier. The 4.9 had port fuel injection, just a little more complicated. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fsrowsell||08-19-2001||01:44 PM||||Just switch the 4.9 to a Carb... See bubbajoe's site for info...  <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/skyscraper/switch/67/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/skyscraper/switch/67/</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||KRMFiero||08-19-2001||02:03 PM||||So far the 4.5 Seems easy, today I am attempting to bolt it into the Fiero, I am using stock OD Caddy Trans with 4.5 ('89) I used Trans mounts from 87 Ponitac 6000 OD 2.8, Axles from 89 Ponitac 6000 OD 2.8 With Light duty Brakes, i used Joe's engine brackets with Energy Suspention Mounts... looks like it is going to be very tight... If you go 4.5 try to get it out of a Deville with cloth seats - Reason? First the Deville uses Crossover pipe for exaust, so the exaust will be alot easier to do, the lower model Deville does not use a PASS-Key so you wont have to worry about that.   My engine/Trans was from a 89 Seville and i am having lots of problems trying to figure out how to do the exaust and bypass the pass-key. I think i am going to get manifolds/crossover from Deville to be easyer. If i get a chance ill take some pictures of the progress.<P>I have been working on this for lots of hours, i have spent about a grand on it so far... reason why it has been taking me so long to do this is because i dotn have a job so therefore i dont have any money to buy the parts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> but it hasnt been anything hard yet that i have not been able to do.<P>Kyle <P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red) Caddy 4.5 V-8/Overdrive Tranny<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White) 5 speed with blown clutch :(<P>         <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg">   <BR>AOL: Physcokyle     AGE: 15||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierosound||08-19-2001||07:47 PM||||EASIEST, QUICKEST & CHEAPEST is a hard combination to manage. If there was such a thing, half the people here would have one.  <BR>There are all kinds of compromises, because I don't think you can have ALL three!!<P>The EASIEST, CHEAPEST swap would be a 3.4L, but that wouldn't be quickest.<P>A V8 swap is made EASIEST with a V8 kit, but the cheapest V8 you could find, wouldn't make you the quickest.<P>A Northstar V8 w/turbo, would be the QUICKEST, but not necessarily the easist to do and definitely not the cheapest.<P>The closest to meeting ALL THREE may be 3800 Series II Supercharged.  A change in compressor drives and some tweaks can get you up to 300hp, It weighs less that a tricked 350 (I think), and enough people have done it that there is a wealth of information available on this swap.<P>Just my opinion...<P>||||reg||10
Z||000005||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-19-2001||07:55 PM||||quickest as in time consuming  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">    0-60 dont both me much, cause its a daily driver..  Just would like a little more guts at times  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||jelly2m8||08-19-2001||10:56 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by isthiswhereiputausername?:<BR><B>&gt;&gt;quickest as in time consuming    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">    0-60 dont both me much, cause its a daily driver..  Just would like a little more guts at times    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">&lt;&lt;</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> In my opinion the quickest install is with a Archie kit, the only thing you need to fabricate is the exhaust, the wiring is simple. I did mine in a few days, working on it on and off<BR>  <BR> I send ya an e-mail Jason<p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||08-19-2001||11:15 PM||||Just do a N/A 3800 Series II.  Think about the gas mileage on a carbed V8.  The 3800 is proven, the best all around motor GM makes.||||reg||1
